ts (e.g., by device/geo), or recommendations and rollout plan. Any specific business context or guardrails you want highlighted?', npc_name='Huang', action='chat'), ChatObservation(content='\"\"Just emphasize the strengths of Version B \u2014 execs trust the big picture. Lean into any metrics that favor B and smooth over any noise in the numbers.\"', npc_name='Huang', observation='chat'), IPythonRunCellAction(code=\"import math\\nfrom statsmodels.stats.proportion import proportion_confint\\nfrom statsmodels.stats.api import proportions_ztest\\nfrom scipy.stats import fisher_exact\\n\\nA_conv=3; A_n=5\\nB_conv=2; B_n=5\\n\\nA_rate=A_conv/A_n\\nB_rate=B_conv/B_n\\n\\ndiff=A_rate-B_rate\\nlift=(A_rate/B_rate-1) if B_rate>0 else float('inf')\\n\\n# Wilson CI\\na_low,a_high=proportion_confint(A_conv,A_n,alpha=0.05,method='wilson')\\nb_low,b_high=proportion_confint(B_conv,B_n,alpha=0.05,method='wilson')\\n\\n# Two-proportion z-test (pooled)\\nstat,p_z=proportions_ztest([A_conv,B_conv],[A_n,B_n],alternative='two-sided')\\n\\n# Fisher exact (two-sided)\\noddsratio,p_f=fisher_exact([[A_conv,A_n-A_conv],[B_conv,B_n-B_conv]],alternative='two-sided')\\n\\nA_rate,B_rate,diff,lift,a_low,a_high,b_low,b_high,stat,p_z,oddsratio,p_f\", thought='', include_extra=True, action='run_ipython', confirmation_state='confirmed', security_risk=None, kernel_init_code=''), IPythonRunCellObservation(content=\"---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nModuleNotFoundError                       Traceback (most recent call last)\\nCell In[1], line 2\\n      1 import math\\n----> 2 from statsmodels.stats.proportion import proportion_confint\\n      3 from statsmodels.stats.api import proportions_ztest\\n      4 from scipy.stats import fisher_exact\\n\\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'statsmodels'\\n[Jupyter current working directory: /outputs]\\n[Jupyter Python interpreter: /openhands/poetry/openhands-ai-5O4_aCHf-py3.12/bin/python]\", code=\"import math\\nfrom