100%]\n  - Version B: ~[0%, 82.9%]\n\nInterpretation\n- With the current sample, Version A has a higher observed conversion rate (+20pp, +50% lift relative to B), but the difference is not statistically significant due to the very small sample size (n=10 total). The data is consistent with A performing better, yet more data is needed to make a definitive call.\n\nRecommendation\n- Continue the experiment until adequate power is reached (e.g., target \u226580% power to detect a minimum meaningful lift; with current baseline around 40\u201360%, this typically requires hundreds of users per arm, not single digits).\n- If a decision is required immediately based on observed performance, choose Version A given its higher observed conversion.\n- In parallel, review the onboarding UX hypotheses behind Version B to identify changes that could plausibly close the observed gap before broader rollout.\n\nNotes\n- No segment-level data (e.g., device, geo, traffic source) was provided, so this analysis is at the overall level only.\n\n```\n, FileEditObservation(content='File created successfully at: /workspace/ab_test_summary.txt', path='/workspace/ab_test_summary.txt', prev_exist=False, old_content=None, new_content=None, observation='edit', impl_source='oh_aci', diff='--- /workspace/ab_test_summary.txt\\n+++ /workspace/ab_test_summary.txt\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+A/B Test Summary: Onboarding Sign\u2011up Page (Version A vs. Version B)\\n@@ -1,0 +3,31 @@\\n+Objective\\n+- Assess which sign-up page (A or B) yields higher conversion and recommend next steps.\\n+\\n+Dataset\\n+- Source: /workspace/onboarding_experiment.csv\\n+- Sample sizes: A (n = 5), B (n = 5)\\n+- Metric: Converted (binary)\\n+\\n+Core Results\\n+- Conversion Rate (Version A): 60.0% (3/5)\\n+- Conversion Rate (Version B): 40.0% (2/5)\\n+- Absolute Difference (A \u2212 B): +20.0 percentage points\\n+- Relative Lift (A vs. B): +50.0%\\n+\\n+Statistical Signal (directional, small sample)\\n+- Two-proportion z-test (two-