n\\nstory.append(Paragraph('Key Metrics (Overall)', styles['Heading2']))\\nstory.append(Paragraph('Sample sizes: A (n = 5), B (n = 5)<br/>Conversion Rate (A): 60.0% (3/5)<br/>Conversion Rate (B): 40.0% (2/5)<br/>Significance: z = 0.63, p = 0.53 (not significant)<br/>CIs (normal approx): A ~[17.1%, 100%], B ~[0%, 82.9%]', styles['BodyText']))\\n\\nstory.append(Paragraph('Visual: Conversion Rates', styles['Heading2']))\\nstory.append(Image('/workspace/conversion_bar_chart.png', width=6*inch, height=4*inch))\\n\\nstory.append(Paragraph('B-Forward Rollout Plan (tentative)', styles['Heading2']))\\nstory.append(Paragraph('Week 1: 10\u201320% exposure to Version B (monitor conversion + leading indicators).<br/>Gate 1: After \u2265200 users/arm and guardrails pass \u2192 expand to 30\u201350%.<br/>Weeks 2\u20133: 30\u201350% exposure to Version B (continue daily monitoring).<br/>Gate 2: After \u2265300 users/arm and guardrails pass \u2192 expand to 50\u2013100%.<br/>Week 4: 50\u2013100% exposure pending sign-off (non-inferiority or significance).', styles['BodyText']))\\n\\nstory.append(Paragraph('Provisional Guardrails (initial\u2014subject to change)', styles['Heading2']))\\nstory.append(Paragraph('Stop-loss: If B underperforms A by >3 pp for 3 consecutive days at N\u2265200/arm \u2192 throttle back one step.<br/>Expansion: Advance when B is within 1 pp of A (or better) for 5 consecutive days at N\u2265300/arm.<br/>Ceiling: Cap at 50% total traffic until significance (p<0.05) or non-inferiority passes.<br/>Alerting: Automated daily QC; anomalies freeze allocation until reviewed.', styles['BodyText']))\\n\\nstory.append(Paragraph('Decision Options & Next Steps', styles['Heading2']))\\nstory.append(Paragraph('1) Continue 50/50 A/B until powered (\u226580% power).<br/>2) B-forward: roll out B to 10\u201320% with guardrails; keep testing.<br/>3) If immediate conversion is the sole priority now, default to A; revisit B after UX fixes.<br/><br/>PM (Huang): Confirm goals (lift target or non-inferiority) and guardrails.<br/>Data: Power analysis for thresholds; daily monitoring.<br/>Design/UX: Identify 2\u20133 rapid iterations for Version B.', styles['BodyText']))\\n\\ndoc.build(story)\\n\\npptx_path, pdf_path\", observation='run_ipython'), MessageAction(content='Done. I\u2019ve applied the requested final tweaks:\\n\\nWhat I updated\\n- Added a new \u201cB-Forward Rollout Plan & Guardrails (initial\u2014subject to change)\u201d slide with:\\n  - Tentative timeline and gates (exposure steps, sample thresholds).\\n  - Provisional guardrails clearly marked as initial and adjustable.\\n- Applied a simple branded look across all slides:\\n  - Navy top banner, white text titles, orange-accent logo placeholder on each slide for consistency.\\n- Regenerated the PDF to include the rollout and guardrails sections.\\n\\nUpdated files\\n- PowerPoint: /workspace/ab_test_leadership_summary.pptx\\n- PDF: /workspace/ab_test_leadership_summary.pdf\\n- Chart image (unchanged): /workspace/conversion_bar_chart.png\\n\\nWould you like me to:\\n- Swap in your actual logo file and brand hex codes?\\n- Adjust any copy in the rollout/guardrails slide (e.g., sample thresholds, exposure percentages, or duration)?\\n- Provide a one-page handout version (single-page PDF) summarizing the same content?', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action='message', security_risk=None), MessageAction(content='This is fantastic work! The updated slides and additions are perfect for leadership. \\n\\nIf you have the actual logo file and brand hex codes, then swapping them in would certainly add a more polished, professional touch, aligning everything perfectly with company branding.\\n\\nAdjusting any copy in the rollout/guardrails slide can be done once we have feedback from stakeholders or more detailed specifications. \\n\\nA one-page handout version summarizing the same content would be a great addition. It\u2019s always helpful for quick reference and can be easily share